§ `String ordering NUL probe`
-- Exercises ordered STRING comparison (<,<=,>,>=) via __l4_str_cmp and
-- equality (==) via __l4_str_eq on two STRING params. The curated cases
-- are branch-crossing on embedded NUL (U+0000): a correct Data.Text
-- comparison keeps the whole string, a NUL-terminated reader truncates.
-- Names are prefixed to avoid the prelude builtins gt/lt/ge/le/eq.
--
-- NOTE: the first @export in a §-sectioned file is emitted as a helper
-- (frontend/schema quirk), so the first DECIDE below is a SACRIFICIAL
-- throwaway; every comparison we actually curate cases for
-- (strGt/strGe/strLt/strLe/strEq) comes after it and is exported for real.

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@export
DECIDE probePrime IF x

GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@export
DECIDE strGt IF a > b

GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@export
DECIDE strGe IF a >= b

GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@export
DECIDE strLt IF a < b

GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@export
DECIDE strLe IF a <= b

GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@export
DECIDE strEq IF a EQUALS b
